% In-memory relational operator: BUCKET

### name: rel.bucket.empty
--- source
LIST() .> BUCKET(_["cat"])
--- expect
none
===

### name: rel.bucket.null
--- source
BUCKET(NULL, _["cat"])
--- expect
none
===

### name: rel.bucket.map-keys
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 1), RECORD("cat", "B", "v", 2), RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 3)) .> BUCKET(_["cat"])
--- expect
tree -{"A"=-{"1"=-{"cat"=t"A", "v"=t"1"}, "2"=-{"cat"=t"A", "v"=t"3"}}, "B"=-{"1"=-{"cat"=t"B", "v"=t"2"}}}
===

### name: rel.bucket.count
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 1), RECORD("cat", "B", "v", 2), RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 3)) .> BUCKET(_["cat"], RECORD("cat", _K, "count", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"cat"=t"A", "count"=t"2"}, "2"=-{"cat"=t"B", "count"=t"1"}}
===

### name: rel.bucket.sum
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 10), RECORD("cat", "B", "v", 20), RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 30)) .> BUCKET(_["cat"], RECORD("cat", _K, "total", SUM(_, _["v"])))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"cat"=t"A", "total"=t"40"}, "2"=-{"cat"=t"B", "total"=t"20"}}
===

### name: rel.bucket.custom-binder
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 10), RECORD("cat", "B", "v", 20)) .> BUCKET(R, R["cat"], RECORD("c", _K, "t", SUM(R, x, x["v"])))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"c"=t"A", "t"=t"10"}, "2"=-{"c"=t"B", "t"=t"20"}}
===

### name: rel.bucket.pipeline.filter-having
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 10), RECORD("cat", "B", "v", 50), RECORD("cat", "A", "v", 30), RECORD("cat", "C", "v", 5)) .> FILTER(_["v"] >= 10) .> BUCKET(_["cat"], RECORD("cat", _K, "total", SUM(_, _["v"]))) .> FILTER(_["total"] >= 40) .> SORT_BY(_["total"], "DESC")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"cat"=t"B", "total"=t"50"}, "2"=-{"cat"=t"A", "total"=t"40"}}
===

### name: rel.bucket.numeric-key
--- source
LIST(RECORD("dept", 10, "v", "x"), RECORD("dept", 20, "v", "y"), RECORD("dept", 10, "v", "z")) .> BUCKET(_["dept"], RECORD("dept", _K, "count", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"dept"=t"10", "count"=t"2"}, "2"=-{"dept"=t"20", "count"=t"1"}}
===

% The key of a bare bucket is an index key (spec §3.3 and §7.4): its scalar
% text, verbatim. A key that is not text or a number is refused with the error
% indexing would give, at the key expression -- never silently collapsed. The
% projected spelling groups by identity (§3.4) and may take any key, because
% no map key has to be made from it. Review 2026-09-15 finding G: the bare
% spelling once folded NULL, LIST and RECORD keys onto one string entry, a
% different one per host, and lost the other rows.

### name: rel.bucket.null-key-is-refused
--- source
LIST(RECORD("c", "x"), RECORD("c", NULL)) .> BUCKET(_["c"])
--- expect
error E_NULL at 1:54
===
### name: rel.bucket.bool-key-is-refused
--- source
LIST(RECORD("c", TRUE)) .> BUCKET(_["c"])
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:36
===
### name: rel.bucket.binary-key-is-refused
--- source
LIST(RECORD("c", FROM_HEX("ff"))) .> BUCKET(_["c"])
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:46
===
### name: rel.bucket.list-key-is-refused
--- source
LIST(RECORD("d", LIST(1, 2)), RECORD("d", LIST(3, 4))) .> BUCKET(_["d"])
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:67
===
### name: rel.bucket.record-key-is-refused
--- source
LIST(RECORD("d", RECORD("x", 1))) .> BUCKET(_["d"])
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT at 1:46
===
### name: rel.bucket.projected-spelling-groups-lists-by-identity
--- note
The projected spelling has no map to key, so a list key is compared as a
value: [1,2] twice is one group, [3,4] another, and _K is the list.
--- source
LIST(RECORD("d", LIST(1, 2), "v", 1), RECORD("d", LIST(1, 2), "v", 2), RECORD("d", LIST(3, 4), "v", 3)) .> BUCKET(_["d"], RECORD("k", _K, "n", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"k"=-{"1"=t"1", "2"=t"2"}, "n"=t"2"}, "2"=-{"k"=-{"1"=t"3", "2"=t"4"}, "n"=t"1"}}
===
### name: rel.bucket.projected-spelling-keeps-null-and-bool-keys
--- source
LIST(RECORD("c", NULL), RECORD("c", ""), RECORD("c", TRUE), RECORD("c", "TRUE")) .> BUCKET(_["c"], RECORD("k", _K, "n", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"k"=-, "n"=t"1"}, "2"=-{"k"=t"", "n"=t"1"}, "3"=-{"k"=TRUE, "n"=t"1"}, "4"=-{"k"=t"TRUE", "n"=t"1"}}
===
### name: rel.bucket.map-spelling-equals-projected-spelling
--- note
For the keys a bare bucket accepts, `BUCKET(k) .> MAP(p)` and `BUCKET(k, p)`
are one value -- which is what lets the SQL translator render them as one
grouped statement.
--- source
A = LIST(RECORD("c", 7, "v", 1), RECORD("c", "7", "v", 2), RECORD("c", 9, "v", 3)); (A .> BUCKET(_["c"]) .> MAP(RECORD("k", _K, "n", COUNT(_)))) EQL (A .> BUCKET(_["c"], RECORD("k", _K, "n", COUNT(_))))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: rel.bucket.key-expression-sees-the-source-key
--- note
Review 2026-09-15 finding Q. Inside the key expression `_K` is the source
element's key -- a record's field name, a list's position -- exactly as in
SORT_BY's key. One host bound it to the position over every source.
--- source
R = RECORD("x", 10, "y", 20, "z", 30); R .> BUCKET(_K)
--- expect
tree -{"x"=-{"1"=t"10"}, "y"=-{"1"=t"20"}, "z"=-{"1"=t"30"}}
===
### name: rel.bucket.rebucket-by-group-key
--- note
The map a bare bucket yields is keyed by the group key, so a second BUCKET
over it can group by `_K`.
--- source
LIST(RECORD("a", 7), RECORD("a", 9), RECORD("a", 7)) .> BUCKET(_["a"]) .> BUCKET(_K, RECORD("k", _K, "n", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"k"=t"7", "n"=t"1"}, "2"=-{"k"=t"9", "n"=t"1"}}
===
### name: rel.bucket.map-of-key-then-sort-by-key
--- note
`_K` inside the MAP is the group key; a SORT_BY(_K) after the MAP reads the
renumbered keys "1", "2". Moving the sort ahead of the MAP would renumber the
buckets before the MAP reads their keys -- every host answered cat 1 / cat 2
here until this pinned it.
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "B"), RECORD("cat", "A"), RECORD("cat", "B")) .> BUCKET(_["cat"]) .> MAP(RECORD("cat", _K, "n", COUNT(_))) .> SORT_BY(_K)
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"cat"=t"B", "n"=t"2"}, "2"=-{"cat"=t"A", "n"=t"1"}}
===
### name: rel.bucket.map-of-key-then-sort-by-mapped-field
--- note
The control: the key reads a field the MAP computed, so the sort already
stayed where it was written.
--- source
LIST(RECORD("cat", "B"), RECORD("cat", "A"), RECORD("cat", "B")) .> BUCKET(_["cat"]) .> MAP(RECORD("cat", _K, "n", COUNT(_))) .> SORT_BY(_["cat"])
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"cat"=t"A", "n"=t"1"}, "2"=-{"cat"=t"B", "n"=t"2"}}
===
